        "description": "Classify raw offset: missing -> {kind:\"missing\",offset:null}; explicit null -> {kind:\"null\",offset:null}; exact integer 2..11 -> {kind:\"integer\",offset:original}; other -> {kind:\"invalid\",offset:null}. No bool/float/coercion/defaults/exceptions. Uses a helper, invokes it at module scope and assigns its returned object to result. Target inputs interface requires selected-runner support; unapproved draft, not submitted or activated.",
        "content": "def classify_offset(value):\n    if 'offset' not in inputs:\n        return {'kind': 'missing', 'offset': None}\n    if value is None:\n        return {'kind': 'null', 'offset': None}\n    valid = type(value) is int and 2 <= value <= 11\n    return {'kind': 'integer', 'offset': value} if valid else {'kind': 'invalid', 'offset': None}\nresult = classify_offset(inputs.get('offset'))"
      }
    }
